   "cite": "occurrence",
   "prompt": "Explain how ammonia can function both as a Brønsted base and as a Lewis base.",
   "answer": {
    "type": "open",
    "generated_by": "source",
    "solution": "Ammonia acts as a Brønsted base because it readily accepts protons and as a Lewis base in that it has an electron pair to donate.<br>Brønsted base: ${\\text{NH}}_{3}+{\\text{H}}_{3}{\\text{O}}^{+}\\;\\longrightarrow \\;{\\text{NH}}_{4}{}^{+}+{\\text{H}}_{2}\\text{O}$<br>Lewis base: ${\\text{2NH}}_{3}+{\\text{Ag}}^{+}\\;\\longrightarrow \\;{{\\text{[H}}_{3}\\text{N}-\\text{Ag}-{\\text{NH}}_{3}]}^{+}$"
   }
  },
  {
